        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f49d84a53ffe4cJW1JRKKzKoxr\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough investigation. Here is the structured report.\n\n---\n\n# P5.2 Chat Page — Codebase Investigation Report\n\nAll paths absolute. No files were modified.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Task spec & hard boundary (read first)\n\n**Task** `P5.2-chat-page` is in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/tasks/prd.json:532-553`. Acceptance bullets:\n- Channel sidebar (workspace/project/custom), thread pane, composer (attach, @mention, emoji picker), threads (inline + dedicated + reply counts), read state (unread dividers, bold channels, mark-read on view).\n- \"Follow existing page/nav conventions (P1.2 nav, Lingui strings, Linaria styling, twenty-ui icons via icon dictionary)\".\n- Depends on `P5.1-chat-model`. Bullets map to `PLAN.md:960-966`.\n\n**Critical boundary — apps cannot add routes.** `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/phases/phase-04-report.md:462-466`:\n> \"Query hooks and provider drivers are **server-side core code** — an app cannot register a post-query visibility hook or a calendar sync driver. Apps can add page-layout widgets, command-menu items, nav items/views, front components, logic functions and (server-registered) search providers. **A full calendar page/route cannot be contributed by an app.**\"\n\nAnd `:524`: \"Apps cannot add routes, query hooks or sync drivers\". Therefore the P5.2 chat **page must be a native `twenty-front` route** (hard-coded), exactly as you said. The a2e-chat app can only ship objects/views/nav/front-components (already done in P5.1).\n\n**Heavy-UI decision order** (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/04-twenty-native-law.md:104-106`):\n> \"(1) metadata views/page layouts; (2) page-layout FRONT_COMPONENT widget; (3) **dedicated front page feature-flagged** — in that order. Log the choice in the phase report.\"\n\nP5.2 is choice (3): a dedicated feature page.\n\n---\n\n## 1. How twenty-front defines full-page routes/pages\n\n### Router entry\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/hooks/useCreateWorkspaceAppRouter.tsx`\n- `:117` `return createBrowserRouter([ ... ])`\n- `:127-141` authenticated shell nesting: `MinimalMetadataGate` → `DefaultLayout` → `MainAppLayoutWithSidePanel` → `getWorkspaceRouteObjectsForSurface(workspaceRouteObjects, 'main')`\n- `:144-269` unauthenticated/onboarding routes under `AuthFlowLayout` / `BlankLayout`.\n\nRoot (no-auth) router is separate: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/hooks/useCreateRootAppRouter.tsx:37-87` (used for `/share/:shareToken`, auth). Workspace pages go in the **workspace** router.\n\nA second renderer for nested/panel routes: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/components/WorkspaceRoutes.tsx:16-25` (`useRoutes(surfaceRouteObjects, location)`).\n\n### The route registry (this is where you add the chat page)\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/utils/createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx`\n- Lazy page imports `:14-54` (pattern: `lazy(() => import('~/pages/...').then(m => ({ default: m.XxxPage })))`).\n- Route array `:72-155`. Representative entry (AI chat), `:122-129`:\n```tsx\n{\n  path: AppPath.AiChat,\n  element: (\n    <LazyRoute>\n      <AiChatPage />\n    </LazyRoute>\n  ),\n},\n```\n- Route entries may carry a `handle` (`WorkspaceRouteObject.ts:5-10`) controlling surfaces:\n```ts\nexport type WorkspaceRouteHandle = {\n  workspaceSurfaces: readonly WorkspaceSurfaceType[];   // 'main' | 'side-panel'\n  isLocationExpandableFromSidePanel?: boolean | ((args) => boolean);\n};\n```\n- `:89-104` example with `handle: { workspaceSurfaces: MAIN_AND_SIDE_PANEL, isLocationExpandableFromSidePanel: true }`.\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/utils/getWorkspaceRouteObjectsForSurface.tsx:12-20`: routes default to **main** if no handle; only declared `side-panel` routes render in the panel. So a chat page will be main-only unless you add `handle`.\n\n### Path enum\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts`\n- `:22` `AiChat = '/chat/:threadId?',`\n- `:27` `OpportunitiesPage = '/objects/opportunities',` `:26` `TasksPage = '/objects/tasks',` — these are canonical URLs that fall through the dynamic `:29 RecordIndexPage = '/objects/:objectNamePlural'`.\n\n⚠️ **Route collision:** `/chat` is already AI chat. A native chat page needs a distinct literal (e.g. `ChatPage = '/discussions'` or `/chat/:channelId?` carefully scoped). Note `chatChannels` records are already reachable at `/objects/chatChannels` via `RecordIndexPage`.\n\nHelper to build URLs: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/utils/navigation/getAppPath.ts:6-29`. Editing `AppPath` requires `npx nx build twenty-shared --skip-nx-cache` (AGENTS.md gotcha).\n\n### Page component convention\nPages live in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/<feature>/<Name>Page.tsx`, **named exports**, thin composition of `@/modules/...` components.\n\nCanonical example, `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/ai-chat/AiChatPage.tsx:41-68`:\n```tsx\nexport const AiChatPage = () => {\n  const shouldOpenAiChatAfterOnboarding = useAtomStateValue(\n    shouldOpenAiChatAfterOnboardingState,\n  );\n  return (\n    <StyledPanel>\n      <AiChatPageHeader ... />\n      <StyledCenteredChatContainer>\n        <AiChatSurfaceContext.Provider value={AI_CHAT_SURFACE.PAGE}>\n          <AiChatTab />\n        </AiChatSurfaceContext.Provider>\n      </StyledCenteredChatContainer>\n    </StyledPanel>\n  );\n};\n```\n\n### Onboarding guard interaction\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/hooks/usePageChangeEffectNavigateLocation.ts:96-226` redirects by `OnboardingStatus`. A new route generally needs no change (it only special-cases onboarding paths / index / record-index / page-layout), but verify if chat should be reachable before completion.\n\n### Tests for the route registry\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/utils/__tests__/createWorkspaceRouteObjects.test.tsx:28-57` — if you add a side-panel-available route, the surface-list assertion `:44-48` will need updating.\n\n---\n\n## 2. P1.2 navigation conventions\n\n### P1.2 report\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/phases/phase-01-report.md:94-121`:\n- **No `workspaceModule` table.** The per-workspace `application` row IS the enable/disable state (created on install, deleted on uninstall). GraphQL surface already complete.\n- New front module `twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/` for A2E cross-app concerns; wired into Settings → Applications.\n- `:118-119` **\"Nav visibility: verified no extension needed — nav items are DB rows owned by the app; uninstall deletes them with the metadata sync; no code change.\"**\n\n`:332` (P1.5, same rule): apps register via metadata/data, not parallel registries.\n\n`:339-371` Bilan anatomy conformance: every app must ship command-menu items (\"Bilan : …\", GLOBAL/pinned) and its front components; the nav item is a DB row.\n\n### Navigation architecture\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/01-codebase-map.md:110-113`: main drawer renders navigation menu items **from the database** (workspace-level `navigationMenuItems`, editable in Settings → Experience); apps can contribute.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/plan/04-twenty-native-law.md:58`: \"Navigation → `defineNavigationMenuItem` (DB-backed nav…) | Forbidden: Hard-coded routers.\" (But note the §0 boundary: a *full page route* is native, the *nav entry* is DB-backed.)\n\n`NavigationMenuItemType` enum `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/NavigationMenuItemType.ts`:\n```ts\nVIEW, FOLDER, LINK, OBJECT, RECORD, PAGE_LAYOUT\n```\n- Display switch: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/navigation-menu-item/display/components/NavigationMenuItemDisplay.tsx:23-83`.\n- `PAGE_LAYOUT` links to native route `/page/:pageLayoutId` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/navigation-menu-item/display/page-layout/utils/getPageLayoutNavigationMenuItemComputedLink.ts:5-15`.\n- Existing a2e-chat nav item is type **VIEW**: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-chat/src/navigation-menu-items/channels.navigation-menu-item.ts:13-19` (`name: 'Discussions'`, `icon: 'IconMessages'`, `position: 130`, `type: VIEW`, `viewUniversalIdentifier: VIEW_IDS.allChannels`). So today the sidebar entry lands on the `chatChannels` record index, **not** a bespoke page.\n\n### product-experience contracts\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/docs/product-experience.md:111-127` (\"Native interaction and visual rules\"):\n- One sidebar; group each app's entries; avoid dumping objects into nav; useful landing page.\n- Reuse metadata table/kanban views and page-layout widgets **before** bespoke components.\n- \"Use the existing side panel for previews and **stable routes for full pages**; back navigation, browser reload and copied links must work.\"\n- Reuse Twenty UI tokens/icons/components; verify light/dark, keyboard focus, narrow screens, loading/empty/error/permission-denied.\n- Host strings use Lingui; hard-coded French JSX is not bilingual.\n- No chat-specific nav contract beyond the above; the \"discussions tab on project/company + side-panel mini-chat\" is a **later** task (`P5.2-record-linked-channels`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. How app-provided front components are hosted\n\nModule: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/front-components/`\n- `components/FrontComponentRenderer.tsx:46-82` — fetches metadata `FindOneFrontComponentDocument` (`:54-56`), resolves SDK client URLs + token, then renders the sandboxed `SharedFrontComponentRenderer` from `twenty-front-component-renderer` (`:177-196`).\n- `hooks/useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts:116-138` builds `executionContext` (workspace/user/record ids) exposed to the app.\n- `states/frontComponentsSelector.ts` — metadata index.\n- Host sites: side panel `modules/side-panel/pages/front-component/components/SidePanelFrontComponentPage.tsx:36-38`; command menu `modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/components/HeadlessFrontComponentRendererEngineCommand.tsx:31-32`; timeline `modules/activities/timeline-activities/rows/components/EventRowDynamicComponent.tsx:88-89`; page-layout widgets.\n\n**There is no generic \"app page shell\".** Front components are embedded islands (side panel / widget / headless command), never routes. The a2e-chat front components are headless commands:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-chat/src/front-components/go-to-chat.front-component.tsx:9-24` — `Command` that calls `navigate(AppPath.RecordIndexPage, { objectNamePlural: 'chatChannels' })`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-chat/src/front-components/create-channel-command.front-component.tsx:18-61` — `CoreApiClient.mutation({ createChatChannels ... })` then navigates to the record.\n\nConclusion: the P5.2 page cannot be an app front component route. Build it natively; keep the existing app command/nav for create/go-to.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Feature module structure (concrete examples)\n\n### Directory layout convention\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/<feature>/`\n```\ncomponents/   (incl. __tests__, __stories__)\nhooks/        (incl. __tests__)\nstates/       (jotai atoms; selectors/ subfolder)\ncontexts/     (component instance contexts)\ngraphql/queries|mutations|fragments/\ntypes/  utils/  constants/  __tests__/\n```\nReference small module: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/` (constants, graphql/{queries,mutations}, hooks/__tests__, components, types). Larger chat-like reference: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/` (components, contexts, graphql, hooks, states, types, utils) — the closest analog to a chat page.\n\n### Jotai state file\nSimple atom — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/states/agentChatInputState.ts:1-6`:\n```ts\nimport { createAtomState } from '@/ui/utilities/state/jotai/utils/createAtomState';\nexport const agentChatInputState = createAtomState<string>({\n  key: 'agentChatInputState',\n  defaultValue: '',\n});\n```\nFactory: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/utilities/state/jotai/utils/createAtomState.ts:53-71` — options `key`, `defaultValue`, `useLocalStorage`, `useSessionStorage`, `useCookieStorage`, `scope: 'routed-flow'`.\n\nComponent-scoped family (for per-panel chat state) — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/states/agentChatMessagesComponentFamilyState.ts:5-13`:\n```ts\nexport const agentChatMessagesComponentFamilyState =\n  createAtomComponentFamilyState<ExtendedUIMessage[], { threadId: string | null }>({\n    key: 'agentChatMessagesComponentFamilyState',\n    defaultValue: [],\n    componentInstanceContext: AgentChatComponentInstanceContext,\n  });\n```\nHooks live in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/utilities/state/jotai/hooks/`: `useAtomStateValue`, `useSetAtomState`, `useAtomComponentFamilyStateValue`, `useSetAtomComponentFamilyState`, etc.\n\n### Component + test\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/components/SettingsA2eSuiteSection.tsx:1-65` (linaria + lingui + twenty-ui Section/H2Title). Test example `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/hooks/__tests__/useA2eSuiteApplications.test.tsx:1-120` (mock `@apollo/client/react`, `renderHook`)